pokeplatinum-widepointers4.patch (tools/pokeplat_gen.py applies it after widepointers3): an address carried in a u32 local.
ov5_021EE320 (the field's billboard texture tables, overlay005) lays three arrays after its header in one Heap_Alloc and
walks to each with `v0 = (uintptr_t)v5 + sizeof(...)`, but v0 was a u32: the host pointers lost their top half
(0x5555'60879120 -> 0x60879120) and the first map object's draw (ov5_021EDFF0) faulted when the field came up after the
new game's intro (pl8). The rule: a local that holds an address is uintptr_t (docs/platinum.md, the crash table).

--- a/src/overlay005/ov5_021ECE40.c
+++ b/src/overlay005/ov5_021ECE40.c
@@ -1791,7 +1791,8 @@
 
 static void ov5_021EE320(UnkStruct_ov5_021ED0A4 *param0, int param1, int param2)
 {
-    u32 v0, v1, v2, v3, v4;
+    uintptr_t v0;
+    u32 v1, v2, v3, v4;
     UnkStruct_ov5_021EDF3C *v5;
 
     v4 = (sizeof(UnkStruct_ov5_021EE294)) * param1;
